==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈheːɐ̯də/|[ˈheːɐ̯də]|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/ˈhɛʁdə/|[ˈhɛʁdə]|[ˈhɛɐ̯də]|lang=de}} {{a|equally common in practice}}
* {{rhymes|eːɐ̯də|ɛʁdə|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|hert}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|herta}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*herdō}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*kerdʰ-||file, row, herd}}. The modern consonantism is [[Central German|Central]] and [[Low German]] (compare {{etyl|gml|de}} {{m|gml|hērde}}). Cognate with {{cog|en|herd}}, {{etyl|da|-}} and {{cog|sv|hjord}}, {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌳𐌰}}.

